{#- app/gui/templates/_access_key_help.html — "How do I create an access key?" (console + CLI),
    shared by Automated setup and /setup/permissions so the two never drift. Callers may set
    `ak_after` ("provisioning" / "the update") and `ak_verb` ("provision" / "update permissions")
    with {% with %} around the include. -#}
<details class="tooldetail" style="margin-top:var(--sp-3)">
  <summary>How do I create an access key?</summary>

  <p class="hint" style="margin-top:var(--sp-3)"><strong>In the AWS Console (manual):</strong></p>
  <ol style="margin:var(--sp-2) 0 0">
    <li>Open the AWS Console → <strong>IAM</strong> → <strong>Users</strong>, and select your
      user (or one with permission to create S3 buckets and IAM users).</li>
    <li>Open the <strong>Security credentials</strong> tab → under <strong>Access keys</strong>,
      choose <strong>Create access key</strong>.</li>
    <li>Choose the <strong>Command Line Interface (CLI)</strong> use case, acknowledge the
      recommendation, then <strong>Create access key</strong>.</li>
    <li>Copy the <strong>Access key ID</strong> and <strong>Secret access key</strong> (the
      secret is shown only once — copy both, or download the .csv), and paste them above.</li>
  </ol>

  <p class="hint" style="margin-top:var(--sp-4)"><strong>With the AWS CLI:</strong></p>
  <div class="cmd" style="margin-top:var(--sp-2)">
    <pre>aws iam create-access-key --user-name &lt;your-iam-user&gt;</pre>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm copy" data-copy="aws iam create-access-key --user-name <your-iam-user>">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <p class="hint">Copy <code>AccessKeyId</code> and <code>SecretAccessKey</code> from the
     output into the fields above (the secret is shown only once).</p>

  <p class="hint" style="margin-top:var(--sp-3)">After {{ ak_after|default('provisioning') }}, remove it:</p>
  <div class="cmd" style="margin-top:var(--sp-2)">
    <pre>aws iam delete-access-key --user-name &lt;your-iam-user&gt; --access-key-id &lt;AKIA…&gt;</pre>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm copy" data-copy="aws iam delete-access-key --user-name <your-iam-user> --access-key-id <AKIA…>">Copy</button>
  </div>

  <p class="hint" style="margin-top:var(--sp-3)">An IAM user can have at most 2 access keys;
     if you're at the limit, delete an unused one first —
     <code>aws iam list-access-keys --user-name &lt;your-iam-user&gt;</code>.</p>

  <p class="hint" style="margin-top:var(--sp-4)">This permanent key is used once to {{ ak_verb|default('provision') }}
     and never stored — delete it afterward. Using SSO / temporary credentials? Paste all
     three fields including the session token instead.</p>
</details>
